/**
 * @page examples NEP Example Programs
 *
 * @section examples_overview Overview
 *
 * The example programs in this directory exercise NEP features: the NEXTCDF-4
 * backend, the UDF format readers, and the disk-bound performance benchmarks.
 * The generic NetCDF teaching examples (classic NetCDF, NetCDF-4, NcZarr,
 * OPeNDAP, parallel I/O, and their Fortran counterparts) moved to
 * [The NetCDF Developer's Handbook repository](https://github.com/captainkirk99/NetCDF_Developers_Handbook).
 *
 * @section examples_categories Example Categories
 *
 * @subsection nextcdf4_c NEXTCDF-4 (C)
 *
 * Located in `examples/nextcdf4/`:
 * - @ref bfloat16.c - Store real GDAS temperature data as NC_BFLOAT16 with the nc_*_bfloat16() functions
 * - @ref bfloat16_perf.c - float32 vs bfloat16 (user-code and internal conversion) size and I/O benchmark, CSV output
 * - @ref bfloat16_io_perf.c - float32 vs bfloat16 write/read benchmark with data already in bfloat16 (no conversion), CSV output
 * - @ref conversion_perf.c - Standard numeric conversion and quantized writes, ten copies and ten repetitions, CSV output; no external plugin required
 * - `plot_conversion_compare.py OFF.csv ON.csv OFF_IO.csv ON_IO.csv PREFIX` plots paired GDAS results; `--numeric OFF.csv ON.csv PREFIX` plots standard conversions. Typed row labels identify HDF5 (OFF) or internal (ON); internal conversion is now permanent and historical CSVs/charts remain unchanged.
 * - @ref make_bfloat16_sample.c - Convert the GDAS sample to a NEXTCDF-4 NC_BFLOAT16 file (used with make_bfloat16_sample.sh)
 * - @ref float16.c - Store real GDAS temperature data as NC_FLOAT16 with the nc_*_float16() functions
 * - @ref float16_perf.c - float32 vs float16 (user-code and internal conversion) size and I/O benchmark, CSV output
 * - @ref float16_io_perf.c - float32 vs float16 write/read benchmark with data already in float16 (no conversion), CSV output
 * - @ref make_float16_sample.c - Convert the GDAS sample to a NEXTCDF-4 NC_FLOAT16 file (used with make_float16_sample.sh)
 *
 * @subsection performance_c Performance Benchmarks (C)
 *
 * Located in `examples/performance/`:
 * - @ref cache_tuning.c - HDF5 chunk-cache tuning effects on read performance
 * - @ref chunking.c - Chunk-shape strategies and I/O performance
 * - @ref chunking_performance.c - Chunking strategies across four layouts (moved from `examples/netcdf-4/` in v4.3.0)
 * - @ref deflate.c - Deflate level and shuffle combinations, disk-bound timing
 * - @ref endianness.c - Byte-order conversion cost
 * - @ref fill_values.c - Fill-value and no-fill write cost
 * - @ref szip.c - SZIP compression (built only when an SZIP library is found)
 * - @ref zstandard.c - Zstandard compression via the HDF5 plugin
 *
 * All NEP benchmark numbers are disk-bound: write time includes fsync,
 * and each read starts with the file dropped from the page cache (see
 * `examples/perf_disk.h`). Reference results are measured with
 * -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo (-O2). Benchmarks run as tests only
 * with `-DNEP_ENABLE_BENCHMARKS=ON`.
 *
 * @subsection udf_readers_c UDF Format Readers (C)
 *
 * - `examples/dicom/dicom_read.c` - Read a DICOM file through the NEP DICOM UDF handler
 * - `examples/pdb/pdb_read.c` - Read a PDB file through the NEP PDB UDF handler
 * - `examples/viz/` - Optional Python visualizations that open NEP UDF files
 *   (FITS, CDF, GeoTIFF, GRIB2, PDS4, mmCIF, PDB, DICOM) with
 *   `netCDF4.Dataset` and write static Matplotlib PNGs. Enable with
 *   `-DNEP_ENABLE_VIZ_EXAMPLES=ON`.
 *
 * @section building_examples Building Examples
 *
 * **CMake:**
 * @code
 * cmake -B build -DNEP_BUILD_EXAMPLES=ON
 * cmake --build build
 * ctest --test-dir build
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section output_validation Output Validation
 *
 * `examples/expected_output/` holds the expected CDL files for the
 * `cache_tuning` and `chunking_performance` validation tests in
 * `examples/performance/`, compared with `ncdump` output via
 * `validate_cdl.sh` (generated from `validate_cdl.sh.in`).
 *
 * @section additional_resources Additional Resources
 *
 * - Generic NetCDF C/Fortran examples:
 *   https://github.com/captainkirk99/NetCDF_Developers_Handbook
 * - Earth-observation mission examples:
 *   https://github.com/captainkirk99/Earth_Observation_in_Practice
 * - NetCDF User Guide: https://docs.unidata.ucar.edu/netcdf-c/current/
 * - CF Conventions: http://cfconventions.org/
 * - NEP Project Documentation: See docs/ directory
 */
